# Day 46 – Build Autonomous Agent Studio

## 60 Days of Claude AI Challenge

Today I built an **Autonomous Agent Studio**, exploring how modern multi-agent AI systems can collaborate, evaluate results, and iteratively improve their outputs.

## What I Learned

- **Agentic AI:** Understanding how specialized AI agents collaborate to solve complex workflows.
- **Iterative Improvement:** Building systems that continuously evaluate and improve their outputs.
- **Workflow Orchestration:** Coordinating planning, execution, evaluation, memory, and safety across multiple AI agents.
- **Production Architectures:** Understanding multi-agent design patterns used in modern AI products.

## What I Built

An interactive **Autonomous Agent Studio** that demonstrates multi-agent workflows and agent orchestration.

### Key Features
- Multi-agent workflow simulation
- Specialized AI agent roles
- Agent orchestration loop
- Execution history
- Success and stopping conditions
- Interactive HTML interface

## Key Takeaway

Autonomous AI systems are not just about a single powerful model. The real potential comes from coordinating specialized agents that can plan, execute, evaluate, and improve together.

